Is there a way (runtime options and/or source patch) to get unix nethack to
recognize terminal cursor key sequences as movement commands (the numberpad
option, although it exists in unix nethack, is apparently insufficient)?
Under X I can change the xterm key translations, but I'd prefer a general
solution.

Implementing this naively would cause the accidental ESC keystroke to drop
the user into a confusing ESC-prefix keymap, ideally it would be best to
timeout if ESC isn't soon followed by an appropriate character.





